.TH "fbd-theme-validate" "" "" ""
.SH "نام (NAME)"
fbd-theme-validate \- Validate feedbackd themes
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.nf
\fBfbd\-theme\-validate\fP [OPTIONS...] <FILE>
.fi
.sp
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
\fBfbd\-theme\-validate\fP parses and validates the given feedbackd theme
file. If the theme specifies parent themes then these are parsed and
validates as well.
.SS OPTIONS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
print help and exit
.TP
.B \fB\-\-version\fP
print version information and exit
.TP
.B \fB\-\-compatible=COMPATIBLE\fP
Specify the device compatible to use. Specify this if you validate a user
theme and want to simulate how it would look like on a device with compatible
\fB\(gaCOMPATIBLE\(ga\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.SS EXAMPLES
.sp
Validate a custom theme in the users home directory the same way as it would be
loaded on a Librem 5:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
fbd\-theme\-validate \-\-compatible=purism,librem5 ~/.config/feedbackd/themes/custom.json
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Validate the device theme for a OnePlus 6T:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
fbd\-theme\-validate /usr/share/feedbackd/themes/oneplus,fajita.json
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS See also
.sp
\fBfeedbackd(8)\fP \fBfbcli(1)\fP \fBfeedback\-themes\fP
